            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.848,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": "one-tenths. So we split a unit from 12 and convert it to 10 one-tenths. Now, the number has 11 units and 14 one-tenths. We subtract 7 onetenths from 14 one-tenths and then subtract 6 units from 11 units."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.152,
            0.812,
            0.176
          ],
          "content": "？ Try computing the difference by converting both lengths to tenths."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.179,
            0.848,
            0.238
          ],
          "content": "？ A Celestial Pearl Danio's length is $2 { \\frac { 4 } { 1 0 } } { \\mathrm { c m } }$ , and the length of a Philippine Goby is $\\frac { 9 } { 1 0 }$ cm. What is the difference in their lengths?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.25,
            0.633,
            0.275
          ],
          "content": "How big are these fish compared to your finger?"
        },
        {
